though LR+ is lo…"], "evidence_against": ["Metabolic syndrome alone does not cause painful erythematous rashes, moderately reducing its plausibility as the sole driver of systemic symptoms."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B4.1", "B4.2"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.5, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "risk_context"}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Neuroendocrine Neoplasm with Cutaneous and Glucometric Manifestations", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "reopened", "prior": 0.05, "posterior": 0.03906249999999999, "danger": 0.3, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Metabolic syndrome alone does not cause painful erythematous rashes, moderately reducing its plausibility as the sole driver of systemic symptoms."], "evidence_against": ["Severe hyperglycaemia and chronic risk factors (obesity, smoking) strongly support diabetic hyperglycaemic crisis (B1) as the primary pathophysiology. Neoplast…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 4.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.5, "interrupt_relevance": 0.4, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "etiology"}, "B1.1": {"id": "B1.1", "label": "Diabetic Ketoacidosis (Type 1/T2-related)", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.30681818181818177, "posterior": 0.30681818181818177, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.0, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "specific_disease", "classification_axis": "mechanism"}, "B1.2": {"id": "B1.2", "label": "Hyperosmolar Hyperglycaemic State (Type 2-related) with Atypical Cutaneous Manifestations", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "live"